<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theobald Wolfe Tone</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1763">1763</a>–<a href="/years/1798">1798</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Wolfe Tone</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theobald Wolfe Tone was an Irish revolutionary, a Protestant lawyer who helped found the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/society-of-united-irishmen">Society of United Irishmen</a> in 1791. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> he persuaded the Directory to send an expedition to Ireland, which reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantry-bay">Bantry Bay</a> in 1796 but could not land. Captured with a French squadron in 1798, he was sentenced to death and died of a self-inflicted wound; he is regarded as the father of Irish republicanism.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/theobald-wolfe-tone.jpg" alt="Theobald Wolfe Tone" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wolfe_Tone.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
